    "result_text": "No dangling references; `MemberIdGenerator` is still legitimately used for `fiscalYearOf`. The implementation is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released **version 2 of the owner identity**. The whole version-2 release is centralized in one new class, and each identifier's derivation mixes in the fixed `V2` tag at its own site:\n\n**New: `util/OwnerIdentityVersion.java`** \u2014 a single home for the release: `TAG = \"V2\"`, `API_VERSION = 2`, `AUDIT_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`, and `tag(base)` which mixes the tag into a derivation input by prefixing it.\n\n**Identifier rederivation (every value changes, no V1 value recurs):**\n- **Region inside identifiers** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.assignMemberId` now embeds `OwnerIdentityVersion.tag(region)` (e.g. `V2NSW`) in the member id.\n- **memberId** \u2014 changes via the V2 region (e.g. `V2NSW2716E6609E7`).\n- **identityKey** \u2014 `IdentityKey.of` now digests the V2-tagged input. Both sides of duplicate detection use it, so detection is unaffected.\n- **householdId** \u2014 `HouseholdIdGenerator.generate` mixes the tag into the digest input, while the household **key** that decides membership is left untouched, so grouping is unaffected.\n\n**User-facing region stays plain (no `V2` tag leaks out):**\n- `OwnerMapper.formatLocality` now derives the region directly from postcode/city (`LocalityResolver.localityOf`) instead of reading it back out of the now-V2 member id \u2014 so `locality` stays `NSW`, `timezone` and `ownerSegment` follow, and the owner segment is recomputed from the version-2 identity.\n- Removed the now-dead `MemberIdGenerator.regionOf` (and its unused import) since nothing reads the region back out anymore.\n\n**Response shape:** OpenAPI gains a new `OwnerIdentity` schema; the top-level `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey` moved under a nested `identity` object, plus a top-level integer `apiVersion` of 2. The mapper builds `identity` via `formatIdentity` and sets `apiVersion` via `formatApiVersion` (using the default-method pattern MapStruct expressions require here). Request fields (`OwnerFields`) are unchanged.\n\n**Audit schema:** `OwnerCreatedEvent` gains `schemaVersion` = 2; its `memberId` naturally carries the V2 identity \u2014 confirmed in the log: `{\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,...,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW2716E6609E7\",...}`.\n\nTests: `Tests run: 4, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
