    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, in-order sequence for `addOwner` (POST `/api/owners`, `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:205-257`). I've marked each step as a **validation** (can reject/short-circuit the request) or a **side-effect** (mutates state on the owner, the datastore, or the outside world).\n\n### Pre-entry\n0. **[validation]** `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the method never runs (line 205).\n\n### Body of `addOwner`\n1. **[side-effect / read]** Read the `Idempotency-Key` request header, trimmed; blank \u2192 `null` (`idempotencyKey()`, line 208).\n2. **[validation / short-circuit]** `replayIfDuplicateKey` \u2014 if a key is present and already recorded, look up the previously created owner and return it with **200 OK**, skipping all creation logic below (lines 209-212, 275-284).\n3. **[side-effect]** `addressResolver.resolve(ownerFieldsDto)` \u2014 mutates the incoming DTO to populate/resolve address fields (line 213).\n4. **[validation]** `ownerFieldsValidator.findMissingOrBlankFields` \u2014 if any required field is missing/blank, throw `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (lines 214-217).\n5. **[side-effect]** Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity via `ownerMapper.toOwner` (line 219).\n6. **[side-effect / read]** Load existing owners with the same last name (case-insensitive), filtered to **active** (non-soft-deleted) owners via `activeOwners` (lines 220-221, 363-365).\n7. **[side-effect]** `owner.setNamesakeCount(...)` \u2014 compute and store namesake count against those same-last-name owners (line 222).\n8. **[side-effect]** `assignHousehold` \u2014 set `householdId` (derived from last name + postcode), compute existing household members, set `householdSize` = members + 1; returns the existing members (lines 223, 295-300).\n9. **[side-effect]** `owner.setTelephone(telephoneNormalizer.normalize(...))` \u2014 normalize telephone (line 224).\n10. **[side-effect]** `owner.setEmail(emailNormalizer.normalize(...))` \u2014 normalize email (line 225).\n11. **[validation]** `disposableEmailDomainValidator.validate(email)` \u2014 reject disposable email domains (line 226).\n12. **[validation]** `postcodeValidator.validate(postcode, city)` \u2014 reject invalid postcode/city combination (line 227).\n13. **[validation]** `rejectIfDuplicateIdentity(owner)` \u2014 load active owners with the same (normalized) telephone; if the full identity key matches an existing owner, throw `DuplicateIdentityException` (lines 228, 350-356).\n14. **[side-effect + conditional validation]** `applyHouseholdRule` (lines 229, 328-341):\n    - If **no** existing household members: run `flagPossibleDuplicate` (sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`).\n    - If there **are** members: set `membershipLevelCap` to the household ceiling; then if `sharesHousehold == true`, clear the possible-duplicate flags; otherwise run `flagPossibleDuplicate`.\n15. **[validation]** `registrationDateValidator.validate(registrationDate)` \u2014 validate the supplied registration date (line 230).\n16. **[side-effect]** If registration date is null, default it to `LocalDate.now()` (lines 231-233).\n17. **[side-effect]** `owner.setRegistrationDate(BusinessDayResolver.toBusinessDay(...))` \u2014 snap the registration date to a business day (line 234).\n18. **[side-effect / read]** Count owners already registered on that (adjusted) registration date (line 236).\n19. **[validation]** If `ownersRegisteredToday >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`, throw `DailyOwnerLimitException` (lines 237-239).\n20. **[side-effect]** `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(...)` \u2014 flag bulk-signup based on the daily count (line 240).\n21. **[side-effect / read]** Count owners in the owner's city (line 241).\n22. **[validation]** If `cityOwnerCount >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`, throw `CityOwnerLimitException` (lines 242-244).\n23. **[side-effect]** `owner.setCapacityWarning(...)` \u2014 flag approaching-capacity based on the city count (line 245).\n24. **[side-effect / read]** `assignMemberId` \u2014 derive a base member id (region/registration date/telephone/last name), read existing ids with that prefix, deduplicate, and set `memberId` (lines 246, 308-318).\n25. **[side-effect / persist]** `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 persist the owner (line 247).\n26. **[side-effect]** If an idempotency key was present, `idempotencyStore.record(key, owner.getId())` (lines 248-250).\n27. **[side-effect]** `ownerAuditLogger.ownerCreated(owner)` \u2014 write an audit-log entry (line 251).\n28. **[side-effect / external]** `welcomeNotifier.welcome(owner)` \u2014 send the welcome notification (line 252).\n29. **[side-effect]** Map the saved owner \u2192 `OwnerDto` and set the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}` (lines 253-255).\n30. Return **201 CREATED** with the DTO and headers (line 256).\n\n### Notes\n- The whole method is **not** annotated `@Transactional` (unlike `deleteOwner`), so the persist, idempotency record, audit log, and welcome notification are not wrapped in a single transaction.\n- The duplicate/identity checks (steps 6, 13) deliberately ignore soft-deleted owners via `activeOwners`.\n\nI did not open the individual validator/normalizer/service classes; the ordering above is exactly as the controller invokes them. If you want the internal rule details of any specific step (e.g. what `postcodeValidator` or `identityDuplicateValidator` actually reject), say which and I'll read that class."
